# raster_resolve_quant — the charter 8 RGB565 resolve quantizer, proved on
# the module zhao_raster_resolve actually instantiates (RASTER.RESOLVE,
# ZH-024). Run with cwd = tests/formal.
#
# TWO TASKS, both required:
#   bmc   — P1 (the shipping quantizer IS min(MAXQ, floor(num/255)) on
#           reference/src/zrender/resolve.cpp's numerator) and P2 (the result
#           can never exceed its RGB565 field — the 2026-08-16 white rail)
#           hold for every input, at BOTH shipping parameter sets. Both are
#           unconditional over free inputs, so depth 2 is the whole property:
#           the harness is combinational and its inputs are unconstrained.
#   cover — the corners the comments claim are REACHABLE: both ends of both
#           channels' ranges, full white landing on the rail, and — the
#           load-bearing one — GREEN'S CLAMP ACTUALLY FIRING (the unclamped
#           floor really is 64 and the rail caught it). Without that cover,
#           a_no_wrap_six would also hold for a quantizer that simply never
#           reaches the top, which is not the theorem claimed.
#
# SCOPE-TOTAL: depth 2 is the FULL state space, not a bound. The harness is
# purely combinational (zhao_raster_quant is two always_comb blocks around
# zhao_raster_div255's one; the only always_ff blocks hold the assert and
# cover statements) and every input is unconstrained, so the reachable state
# set is identical at every step. The input parametrisation is likewise total
# rather than sampled: v is a u8 because the working colour channel IS a u8,
# and B is 0..15 because the 4x4 Bayer matrix's entries are exactly 0..15 —
# free (v, B) is all 4,096 inputs the block can ever be handed. There is no
# horizon for a scope guard to assert.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT PROVE, stated plainly. The Bayer MATRIX itself (which of
# the 16 values sits at which (y&3, x&3)), the absolute phase arithmetic, the
# tile walk, the skid FIFO credit rule and the CRC are NOT proved here: they
# are covered by the differential lanes against zref::TileResolve
# (raster_resolve_directed's 1,024-tile channel sweep and 16-phase grid, plus
# raster_resolve_random) and by the mutation evidence in the contract. What
# IS proved is the arithmetic every one of those pixels flows through.
#
# Frontend: read_slang (the lane choice since W2.3). No package dependencies:
# zhao_raster_quant.sv and zhao_raster_div255.sv are self-contained, so
# nothing is staged or copied.

[tasks]
bmc
cover

[options]
bmc: mode bmc
bmc: depth 2
cover: mode cover
cover: depth 2
expect pass

[engines]
smtbmc boolector

[script]
read_slang --top raster_resolve_quant_fv zhao_raster_div255.sv zhao_raster_quant.sv raster_resolve_quant_fv.sv
prep -top raster_resolve_quant_fv

[files]
../../fpga/rtl/raster/zhao_raster_div255.sv
../../fpga/rtl/raster/zhao_raster_quant.sv
raster_resolve_quant_fv.sv
